Aim: To build a Java application using Gradle in IntelliJ IDEA and host a static website using GitHub Pages.
Steps to perform
1. Open IntelliJ IDEA.
2. Click New Project.
3. Select Java and choose Gradle as the build system.
4. Select JDK 17.
5. Choose Groovy DSL or Kotlin DSL.
6. Set the Group ID, such as com.example.
7. Click Create.
8. Open build.gradle and add the configuration and dependencies provided in the manual.
9. Inside src/main/java/com/example, create Main.java.
10. Enter the Java program.
11. Open the Gradle tool window using View → Tool Windows → Gradle.
12. Run the application from the Gradle tasks or terminal:
gradle run


13. Create a folder named docs inside the project root.
14. Inside docs, create index.html.
15. Add the HTML, CSS and images required for your website.
16. Open GitHub and create a new repository.
17. Open the terminal in IntelliJ IDEA.
18. Execute:
git init
git add .
git status
git commit -m "first commit"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin YOUR_REPOSITORY_URL
git push -u origin main


19. Open your GitHub repository.
20. Click Settings → Pages.
21. Under Build and deployment, select Deploy from a branch.
22. Choose the main branch and /docs folder.
23. Click Save.
24. Once GitHub Pages finishes publishing, click Visit Site.
